<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Telegram listener.

  Uses the RESOLVED interpreter path, not the /usr/local/bin/python3 symlink:
  launchd refused to exec through the symlink with EX_CONFIG (78) and an empty
  log -- the program never started, so nothing explained why. The agent job
  survived the same plist shape only because its Program is /bin/zsh, a real
  system binary.

  Invokes python DIRECTLY, no `zsh -lc` wrapper: under launchd a login shell
  sources the user profile in a minimal environment and can exit 78 (EX_CONFIG)
  before python ever starts, which produces an empty log and no clue. Fewer
  moving parts is worth more here than shell convenience.

  No WorkingDirectory, absolute script path: launchd failed the spawn with
  EX_CONFIG (78) and an EMPTY log because it could not chdir into ~/Documents,
  which is TCC-protected. The program never started, so nothing said why.
  tg.py derives its paths from __file__, so it never needed a cwd.

  KeepAlive restarts it if it dies -- including the deliberate exit tg.py makes
  when its own source changes, so an edit picks up automatically.
  ThrottleInterval stops a crash-loop from spinning.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>com.sudhanshu.tradingbot.telegram</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/Library/Frameworks/Python.framework/Versions/3.14/bin/python3</string>
    <string>/Users/sudhanshukushwaha/Documents/Repo/trading-bot/tg.py</string>
    <string>--listen</string>
  </array>
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict><key>PYTHONUNBUFFERED</key><string>1</string></dict>
  <key>KeepAlive</key><true/>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key><true/>
  <key>ThrottleInterval</key><integer>15</integer>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/sudhanshukushwaha/Documents/Repo/trading-bot/data/telegram.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/sudhanshukushwaha/Documents/Repo/trading-bot/data/telegram.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
